<title>PHILIPPINES: Itogon-Suyoc temporarily shuts mines.</title>
<headline>Itogon-Suyoc temporarily shuts mines.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine gold and silver miner Itogon-Suyoc Mines Inc said on Wednesday its board of directors had decided to suspend mining operations for a period of three to six months starting on October 16.</p>
<p>In a disclosure to the Philippine Stock Exchange Inc, the mining firm said the shutdown was due to &quot;continuing and increasingly aggravating losses.&quot;</p>
<p>Itogon-Suyoc reported a net loss of 28.066 million pesos for the first half of 1996.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 fax 8176267</p>
</text>
